Hmm?  I don't recall kobolds or giant beetles having poison attacks,
but they sure are poisonous if eaten.

In any case, IIRC poison dart frogs secrete their poison onto their
skin.  Perhaps they could have a passive poison attack: "You hit the
poison dart frog.  The frog's poison splatters all over you!"
Certainly they should be lethal to creatures with bite attacks.

But the real challenge here is that there certainly should be a way to
poison weapons with them, as if by dipping into a potion of sickness.
Maybe by #rubbing the weapon on the corpse?  And dipping the corpse
into a potion of water or fruit juice (or maybe any potion at all?)
should turn it into poison.  And any projectiles that hit them should
become poisoned automatically.

That said, all this poison dart frog business is secondary -- just
having plain ol' ordinary frogs hopping about would be cool enough.

